      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "The authors report a case of coronary arteriomegaly in a patient with Ehlers-Danlos syndrome and multiple aneurysms who presented with myocardial infarction. Coronary arteriography revealed distal \"pruning\" of vessels without occlusive disease. Fibroblast cultures excluded Ehlers-Danlos syndrome types IV and VII. Literature review suggests this may represent a previously unidentified vascular syndrome."},
